>
> While I have said recently that COI broda == COI le broda or COI la broda 
> depending on context, I would be completely fine with it being explicitly 
> defined as the former. However I will say that requiring this will not 
> prevent jokes--for example {coi le xalbo} when speaking to {la xalbo} is 
> often a reasonable description, which would make {coi xalbo} also a 
> reasonable greeting phrase.
>

di'u sounds like a step back to something like TLI Loglan that had not 
requirement to use {doi} (or whatever it was called)
Absolutely not connected things but of the same level of stupidity.


> mi'e la latro'a mu'o
>
